{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":16,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 16:1"},"Then Job answered and said, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 16:2"},"I have heard many such things: miserable comforters ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," ye all. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 16:3"},"Shall vain words have an end? or what emboldeneth thee that thou answerest? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 16:4"},"I also could speak as ye ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["do:"]}," if your soul were in my soul’s stead, I could heap up words against you, and shake mine head at you. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 16:5"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["But"]}," I would strengthen you with my mouth, and the moving of my lips should asswage ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["your grief. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 16:6"},"Though I speak, my grief is not asswaged: and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["though"]}," I forbear, what am I eased? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 16:7"},"But now he hath made me weary: thou hast made desolate all my company. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 16:8"},"And thou hast filled me with wrinkles, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," is a witness ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["against me:"]}," and my leanness rising up in me beareth witness to my face. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 16:9"},"He teareth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["me"]}," in his wrath, who hateth me: he gnasheth upon me with his teeth; mine enemy sharpeneth his eyes upon me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 16:10"},"They have gaped upon me with their mouth; they have smitten me upon the cheek reproachfully; they have gathered themselves together against me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 16:11"},"God hath delivered me to the ungodly, and turned me over into the hands of the wicked. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 16:12"},"I was at ease, but he hath broken me asunder: he hath also taken ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["me"]}," by my neck, and shaken me to pieces, and set me up for his mark. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 16:13"},"His archers compass me round about, he cleaveth my reins asunder, and doth not spare; he poureth out my gall upon the ground. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 16:14"},"He breaketh me with breach upon breach, he runneth upon me like a giant. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 16:15"},"I have sewed sackcloth upon my skin, and defiled my horn in the dust. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 16:16"},"My face is foul with weeping, and my eyelids is the shadow of death; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 16:17"},"Not for ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["any"]}," injustice in mine hands: also my prayer ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," pure. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 16:18"},"O earth, cover not thou my blood, and let my cry have no place. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 16:19"},"Also now, behold, my witness ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," in heaven, and my record ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," on high. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 16:20"},"My friends scorn me: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["but"]}," mine eye poureth out ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["tears "]},"unto God. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 16:21"},"Oh that one might plead for a man with God, as a man ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["pleadeth "]},"for his neighbour! ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 16:22"},"When a few years are come, then I shall go the way ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["whence "]},"I shall not return. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 16:22"}]}]}
